---
// Export guide: Martialytics → BeltManager (#30). US English (Martialytics' customers are
// mostly US schools). Every Martialytics step is sourced to Martialytics' own help center,
// accessed 7 Nov 2026. No price claims, no claims about why people leave.
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import BreadcrumbsEnhanced from '../../components/seo/BreadcrumbsEnhanced.astro';
import ImportSteps from '../../components/switch/ImportSteps.astro';
import Sources from '../../components/switch/Sources.astro';
import RelatedGuides from '../../components/switch/RelatedGuides.astro';

const ACTIVE_URL = 'https://intercom.help/martialytics/en/articles/4222112-how-to-export-a-list-of-active-students';
const INACTIVE_URL = 'https://intercom.help/martialytics/en/articles/4222042-how-to-export-a-list-of-inactive-students';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="How to Export Your Students from Martialytics"
  description="Step-by-step: download your Martialytics Student List as a CSV, check the columns, and import it into BeltManager. Sourced to Martialytics' own help center, November 2026."
  type="article"
  schemaType="Article"
  publishedDate="2026-11-07"
  modifiedDate="2026-11-07"
  lang="en-US"
>
  <BreadcrumbsEnhanced
    site="beltmanager"
    items={[
      { label: 'Home', href: '/' },
      { label: 'Switching guides', href: '/switch/' },
      { label: 'Martialytics', href: '/switch/martialytics/' },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="bg-gradient-to-br from-brand-navy to-gray-900 text-white py-14">
    <div class="container-custom max-w-3xl">
      <span class="inline-block bg-brand-red/20 text-brand-red-light px-3 py-1 rounded-full text-sm mb-4">Switching guide</span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl md:text-5xl font-bold mb-4">How to export your students from Martialytics</h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-gray-300">
        Martialytics lets you download your student list as a CSV file yourself, without a support ticket. Here's how, what to check in the file, and how to bring it into BeltManager.
      </p>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-400 mt-4">Checked against Martialytics' help center on November 7, 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section bg-white">
    <div class="container-custom max-w-3xl">
      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6">Export your active students</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">Martialytics' help article <em>How To: Export a list of Active Students</em> [1] gives three steps:</p>
      <ol class="space-y-3 text-gray-700 mb-8 list-decimal pl-6">
        <li>Open the filters at the top of your <strong>Student List</strong> and click <strong>Reset</strong>.</li>
        <li>Make sure the <strong>Active Students</strong> toggle is on, then click <strong>Apply Filters</strong>.</li>
        <li>Click the <strong>Export</strong> button (the down-arrow icon) at the bottom of the Student List. A CSV file of your active students downloads.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6">Inactive students are a separate export</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        To export former students, Martialytics' help center [2] says to reset the filters, toggle <strong>Active Students</strong> off, toggle <strong>Inactive Students</strong> on, apply the filters, and export the same way.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-8">
        You may not need that file. BeltManager imports students as <em>active</em> or <em>trial</em>, so we suggest starting with the students who train with you now. Keep the inactive file somewhere safe in case anyone comes back.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-3xl font-bold text-brand-navy mb-6">Open the file before you import it</h2>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        Martialytics' help article doesn't list which columns the export contains; it describes the file only as your active student data. So open it in Excel or Google Sheets and look for:
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2 text-gray-700 mb-6 list-disc pl-6">
        <li>first and last name (in two columns, or one you need to split);</li>
        <li>date of birth, which BeltManager needs for every student;</li>
        <li>parent or guardian name, email and phone for students under 18;</li>
        <li>the student's current rank, if it's there, to map to <code>Current belt</code>;</li>
        <li>the program or class they attend, to map to <code>Group</code>.</li>
      </ul>
      <p class="text-gray-700 mb-4">
        If a column you need isn't in the export, add it by hand in the spreadsheet before importing. Renaming headings to BeltManager's (listed below) is optional, but it means the columns match themselves.
      </p>
      <p class="text-gray-700">
        <strong>Before you cancel Martialytics:</strong> check your cancellation terms with Martialytics in writing, and keep your billing running there until your families are set up in BeltManager.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <ImportSteps variant="us" from="Martialytics" />

  <Sources
    heading="Sources"
    accessed="Martialytics help center pages accessed November 7, 2026"
    items={[
      { label: 'Martialytics: How To: Export a list of Active Students', url: ACTIVE_URL },
      { label: 'Martialytics: How To: Export a list of Inactive Students', url: INACTIVE_URL },
    ]}
  />

  <section class="bg-gray-50 py-8">
    <div class="container-custom max-w-3xl text-gray-700">
      Running a school in the US? See <a href="/us/" class="text-brand-red hover:underline">BeltManager for US martial arts schools</a>.
    </div>
  </section>

  <RelatedGuides current="/switch/martialytics/" />
</BaseLayout>
